  "notes": "v3 of the two-beam 2923 nm / HeNe layout: v2's beam paths, mounted from the hole grid and calibrated for 57 um.\nEvery mirror is a post-centred KM100CP in a hole (it reflects at the hole centre); BX7/BX8 stand on identical\nmachined risers bolted to holes; KE1 is the MRAK25 in a machined holder on a post at (12.5, 9.5), its edge 4.5 mm\nahead of the post, so beams fed along x = 12.5 land 4.5 mm either side of it and leave 9.0 mm apart.\nCheckpoints: IR1/IR2 after the pellicles (with each BE02R's input port), IR3 on the top zigzag, IR4/IR5 on the\nfeeds into KE1, and the dual-pinhole target at (8.5, 9.5), where the beams pass 3.92 mm either side of the row.\nCo-alignment: seat M9 (top) or M8 (bottom); the sample leaves down x = 7.29 through the bottom panel.\nSpots: M27 (top) and M30 (bottom), 10 um per mrad. Pupil: M31 against M27, M28 against M30, M22 + M23 together.\nCustom parts: docs/custom-parts.md. Procedure and knob table: docs/v3-layout.md.",
